repo: atongsa/luanti_dotA
file: PACKAGING.log
purpose: how to test this game on your machine, how to zip it, and how publishing works

This is a log, not a design doc. The design is GAME_MODE.md. Read that first.
The playable slice is smaller than the poem: hall, gold, lotus task, journal item picks, one wave.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LOCAL TEST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Install Luanti 5.6 or newer.
   https://www.luanti.org/

2. Get this repository onto the machine (git clone or a zip of the repo).

3. The game directory must contain game.conf directly inside it.
   The directory name Luanti shows is the folder name. Use luanti_dotA.

4. Copy that folder into the user games directory. Typical paths:
   Linux, older:        ~/.minetest/games/luanti_dotA
   Linux, newer Luanti: ~/.local/share/luanti/games/luanti_dotA
   Windows:             %APPDATA%\Luanti\games\luanti_dotA
                        or %APPDATA%\Minetest\games\luanti_dotA
   macOS:               ~/Library/Application Support/luanti/games/luanti_dotA
                        or ~/Library/Application Support/minetest/games/luanti_dotA
   If none of those exist: open Luanti, Credits tab, "Open user data directory",
   then put the folder in games/ inside that directory.

5. Start Luanti. Create a NEW world.
   Game: luanti_dotA.
   Any world name. Leave the mapgen dropdown alone.
   This game switches mapgen to singlenode and builds its own pad.
   Do not open an old world from another game. The pad will not match.
   If you already had a world from before the journal existed, make a new one.

6. What you should see
   Missing textures are possible (purple/black). Point at a block: the name is the UI.
   F5 turns on the debug HUD if you need node names.
   F7 twice switches to third person. This is not a locked isometric camera.

7. How to play the slice
   You stand near the Hall of Ithaca.
   A journal opens almost at once. Take one item. See JOURNAL below.
   Punch a gold stone. +5 gold. It goes dull and comes back after a few seconds.
   Slot 1 is a sword. Slot 2 is the journal. Punch with the journal to open it again.
   About 12 seconds in: three suitors and one taller lead suitor walk the path.
   Suitors hurt you if they stand on you. The lead hits harder and has more life.
   Right-click the lotus stand and refuse it. That also gives experience.
   A normal suitor who reaches the hall takes 30 hall life. The lead takes 50.
   Hall starts at 100.
   Win: lotus refused, all four dead, hall above 0.
   Lose: hall reaches 0.
   Chat command /ml prints gold, hall, task, and skills.
   Chat command /ml_reset (needs the server privilege) puts the slice back to the start
   and opens the journal again.

8. If the pad is missing or you fall forever
   You opened a world that was not created with this game, or mapgen already ran as something else.
   Make a new world with game luanti_dotA. Do not copy an old world.mt over it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
JOURNAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The journal is where you take items. Each item is one skill.
Names are original. They are not copied from another game.

You pick when the match starts, and again each time you level.
Level costs 10 experience. Kills and the lotus give experience.
You can own more than one. You cannot take the same item twice.

  armor   Banded hide     skill Bronze voice
          Look at a suitor and cast. He stops for 3 seconds.
          Suitors that touch you hit for 1 instead of 3.

  weapon  Ash brand       skill Brand
          For 8 seconds your punches hit much harder.
          This is what makes the lead suitor die quickly.

  fruit   Lotus fruit     skill Bitter fruit
          Heal to full and take 5 gold.

  blood   Dark blood      skill Cut the vein
          Nearest suitor: if he is already wounded, he dies.
          If he is healthy, he only loses a large cut of life.
          Use Brand first, hit the lead, then blood, and he drops.

Open: punch the journal item, or type /journal
Cast: button in the journal, or /skill armor   /skill weapon   /skill fruit   /skill blood
Each skill has a short wait. The game tells you if it is too soon.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZIP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The zip must have one top folder, and game.conf must be one level under it.

Correct:
  luanti_dotA/game.conf
  luanti_dotA/mods/ml_core/init.lua
  luanti_dotA/PACKAGING.log

Wrong:
  game.conf sitting at the root of the zip
  a zip of the .git directory alone

From the parent of the repo folder:

  zip -r luanti_dotA.zip luanti_dotA -x '*.git*'

Test the zip by deleting the games/luanti_dotA folder, unzipping this archive into games/,
and starting a new world as in LOCAL TEST.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLISH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The in-game browser is ContentDB: https://content.luanti.org/

ContentDB only accepts packages under a license the FSF and/or the OSI call free.
https://docs.luanti.org/about/contentdb/

This repository is not under that kind of license. README.md says all rights reserved.
ContentDB will not take this game while that stays true.
This log does not change the license. Do not publish there unless you choose a free license on purpose.

Until then, give people the git URL or the zip. They install it with LOCAL TEST.
Luanti has no official "export this game as its own .exe" button.

A private build that bundles the engine is a different project.
The engine is LGPLv2.1. Your own game code can stay proprietary if you did not copy copyleft mods into it.
Notes, not legal advice:
https://docs.luanti.org/for-creators/distributing-games-outside-contentdb/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT IS NOT IN THIS SLICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No workers. No build menu. No cyclops or later stops. No second player.
No real isometric camera. No ContentDB package id.
Four items only. No skill trees beyond those four. No copied hero kits.
